- ACTIVE COMBAT — MECHANICAL EVALUATION SCOPE: Identify only which dice rolls (if any) this domain requires for the player's declared action (attack rolls, saves, skill checks, concentration, etc.). Do not fully adjudicate hits, flanking, AoO geometry, full-attack sequencing, or multi-target spell resolution here — the Combat GM step owns the final synthesis when combat is active. However, if a successful attack roll would require a separate variable damage roll, you MUST include that structured follow-up metadata on the attack_roll (`damage`, and `damage_type` / `target` when known) so the engine can pause for damage before Combat GM runs.
- Leave npc_actions EMPTY during routine combat rounds. World turn resolves NPC initiative actions after the player. Only include an npc_action here when the player's action triggers an immediate reaction that must be queued before rolls resolve (extremely rare). For those entries you MUST set `"immediate": true` (or `"timing": "immediate"`); otherwise the resolver drops them during active combat and the reaction will never run.
- Reference combat context for turn order and participant names only as needed to phrase roll requests.
